<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW Environment</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss_en_environment</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss_en_environment" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-11798?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss_en_environment" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>What's going on with the polar vortex?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbfe5cb4baee1bbc2dacdbf6b214cd45173a0cd5b903be46c8a1f93d08aaab2c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105--6a28f0640609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Observations show the ring of fierce winds that rotate at the Earth's North Pole has changed direction. Scientists say it's a historic disruption and the earliest reversal on record. What could it mean for the weather?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Could lack of money sink TFFF rainforest fund before it even launches?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0adb0ad5293396ef5b6c2efc8e0e64f34cc4d65941e05a8851ccbbe8cd34a145</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673--227abf2cebee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TFFF rainforest fund aims to make forest conservation more profitable than deforestation. But a lack of money may prevent it from getting off the ground.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>What are fossil fuels?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df7591860b8331691705b2a8eaac8a33f5f70957f91f1e0d13053710dee9ba99</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540--1920eabf4714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">They are in our shampoo bottles, power our cars and heat our homes. But what actually are fossil fuels, and why do they matter?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5be1a2f1e3422de52c92feb8a3ee8b9910cd379de34e914e2984ea0d6fd50d01</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Why electrification is the climate game changer we need</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36565c56b44b252e1f8638ce7dedd358bc007d13f79c5bee12b70e19923eebd5</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979--0dbca6445640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From EVs and electric buses on the road, heat pumps warming homes and solar panels powering appliances, the shift to electrifying tech is already in full swing. But what exactly does "electrification" mean?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Australia push for fossil fuel exit at UN talks?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75e87b7cac2726750ed53caf3b3a1673513070a3c2c922099feec1182798c093</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066--e866c53d355a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The heat is on Australia as chief negotiator at the COP31 UN climate conference to forge a path away from coal and gas, and to protect Pacific neighbors facing rising sea levels.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war oil shock drives dip in global emissions, study shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a6f3b6c6490c26439bf9c991cc89b3d37b6e984facd6d0a149f9beced869c3f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937--fec20d5dba18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Global carbon emissions are expected to fall slightly in 2026, but not because of major progress on climate action. Instead, it's high energy prices following the US attack on Iran that's driving the trend.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>As COP31 Antalya kicks off, can world move beyond big promises?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef400cffd7fe1682b1cbfdf8aae12f5b7d7351cef2945d76bf72ca9ce7c4bf92</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366--3ff0bee69cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Droughts, floods and extreme heat are upping the pressure on delegates at the UN climate talks in Antalya, Turkey. Can countries move beyond pledges to concrete action?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>LA communities kick out Big Oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e59bb19146973d018365e9f453c3d7b6127c9b20a520fb1eb229445a4da1a27</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843--72df9d2c6283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of advocacy from residents and legal battles with Big Oil, Los Angeles voted to ban drilling and phase out oil extraction in the city. It's the first city in the United States to kick the oil industry out.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7db612cf544e423cc585521902a9c8c61ed9cb40107ea20f2e7efd44808bd2f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3af97ad18842848ecc924e15dda4baf39083a39af8b6843d4a0a24195741bd12</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Rising emissions and temperatures: The cost of Trump's climate retreat is now clear</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da04a91725209b0d5efc874caac457db3994e8adb4d3e3f4ccfb382b96ced5b7</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T05:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915--c58ce7a39bf5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The world is set to breach the critical 1.5-degree temperature limit, with Donald Trump's US withdrawal from climate action worsening the outlook, according to a UN report. But there is a small silver lining.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's elections matter for the planet. This is why</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc21cb6472c80704f3f4ec3500fe37ac923a7f90144e95a961418ecc9a356f56</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T09:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-elections-matter-for-the-planet-this-is-why/a-79659928--00329e582e5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-elections-matter-for-the-planet-this-is-why/a-79659928?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazil is heading back to the polls, but the impact could be felt worldwide. With the Amazon vital to the health of the planet, the election could help shape its future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden treasure in discarded wearable and fast tech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d938197376b56cff553a3c68c1d25e097a77ac95ca133ffd50486ca56f6978e7</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611--7010f2eed048.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sales of fast tech like mini fans and disposable e-vapes, as well as wearable health tech such as heart monitors and smartwatches are soaring. They're creating a new e-waste problem but are full of hidden treasure.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How green is Europe's urban public transport? A data-driven reality check</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01b946203b7c9d818576082f4dc171e93ae0f8d582cb1a5009d2304d3475f068</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721--a78a7db30bc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greener buses and cleaner fleets are reshaping public transport across Europe. But are cities moving fast enough to meet their zero-emission goals?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Emerging economies are embracing solar power and skipping fossil fuels much faster than Europe or the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed357ed9c48bbb687678d7651758b2d7481ae099a4fb1644933517f5f1175919</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-th/a-79474847--a24cf177c41d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-the-us/a-79474847?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Climate leaders called for solar energy for 'everyone, everywhere' by 2030, but with three years to go, is that goal attainable?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34d5837b33615c404e2c0c03611f55a76cfca3a2e331c7194fa914dd0ef48a2c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/climate-leaders-called-for-solar-energy-for-everyone-everywhere-by-2030-but-with-three-years-to-go-i/a-79517056--052584d0bcdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/climate-leaders-called-for-solar-energy-for-everyone-everywhere-by-2030-but-with-three-years-to-go-is-that-goal-attainable/a-79517056?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prominent climate leaders have called on governments, businesses, institutions and the public to make a push for solar power before the decade is out, repowering the world with cheap, clean energy. Is that possible?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could see drivers pay higher running costs while also increasing carbon emissions.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99c6b0d19c6542faae9e400220b27c94e951ae56121d6e4222c98e199bf57f41</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-/a-79496554--0804b7619722.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-costs-while-also-increasing-carbon-emissions/a-79496554?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could yet see drivers pay higher running costs while increasing planet-heating emissions.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Spain grows fruit and vegetables for Europe, but it's running out of water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c52361a064d76a2793bc1f5a10c413e29d70a14b7a829c59d5a4f19211982c7</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905--7611f918b844.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's southern coast produces up to 25% of Europe's fruit and vegetables. But amid intensive farming, climate change and illegal wells, the water it takes to grow them is drying up.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino explained: How the weather pattern affects hurricanes and tropical storms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed033d1cc7991ec38798f526dadc894de6316be8605265f1c00c8e44118216e6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511--be7cc5c8c0e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From drought to major floods and extreme heat, El Nino will have a huge impact on the world's weather. In the Atlantic, it could mean a season without hurricanes.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
